First, I need to figure out how much beeswax he needs to make 20 candles. Since one pound makes 10 candles, then for 20 candles, he would need 20 divided by 10, which is 2 pounds of beeswax. Right? Because 1 pound = 10 candles, so 2 pounds would be 20 candles. That makes sense.

Now, the cost for one pound of beeswax and wicks is $10. So for 2 pounds, the total cost would be 2 times $10, which is $20. So his total cost is $20.

Then, he sells each candle for $2.00. If he sells 20 candles, his total revenue is 20 multiplied by $2.00. That would be 20 * 2 = $40. 

